    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Clean an email list before you send\n\nThis flow verifies a list in one batch and splits it into addresses that are safe to send to and ones to review first.\n\n**Setup**\n1. On the **Verify Batch** node, add an *EmailSherlock API* credential. Start with an `es_test_` sandbox key so every branch runs deterministically with no credits spent, then switch to an `es_live_` key for real addresses.\n2. Replace the sample addresses with your own, or map an expression like `{{ $json.recipients }}` from an earlier node (a spreadsheet read, a CRM export, a form).\n\nThe sample addresses each hit a different sandbox result (valid, invalid, disposable, role, catch-all, unknown), so you can see the split before you wire in your own data.\n\nGet a free key at emailsherlock.com.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "9b1f2a3c-0006-4a10-8b00-000000000006",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -160]
    }
  ],
